<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Javascript on cesun.life</title><link>https://example.org/tags/javascript/</link><description>Recent content in Javascript on cesun.life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 08 Jan 2026 10:38:14 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/tags/javascript/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Measuring Browser and DOM Dimensions</title><link>https://example.org/dom-dimensions/</link><pubDate>Thu, 08 Jan 2026 10:38:14 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/dom-dimensions/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Browser APIs expose several coordinate systems because a screen, browser
window, viewport, document, and element answer different measurement
questions. Choosing an API by name alone can therefore produce scrollbar,
rounding, or scrolling errors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="window-screen-and-viewport-measurements"&gt;
 Window, Screen, and Viewport Measurements
 &lt;a href="#window-screen-and-viewport-measurements" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;table&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;API&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Measurement&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;window.innerWidth&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;innerHeight&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Layout viewport, including a rendered classic scrollbar&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;window.outerWidth&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;outerHeight&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Browser window&amp;rsquo;s outside dimensions&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;screen.width&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;screen.height&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Screen dimensions in CSS pixels&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;screen.availWidth&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;screen.availHeight&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Screen space excluding reserved operating-system areas&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;document.documentElement.clientWidth&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;clientHeight&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Layout viewport excluding a classic scrollbar&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CSS pixels are logical units. A CSS pixel can cover multiple device pixels on
a high-density display, so &lt;code&gt;screen.width&lt;/code&gt; does not necessarily equal the
panel&amp;rsquo;s physical pixel count.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sizing HTML Canvas Elements</title><link>https://example.org/canvas-size/</link><pubDate>Mon, 12 Aug 2024 15:47:28 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/canvas-size/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;An HTML canvas has two sizes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;width&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;height&lt;/code&gt; attributes define its drawing buffer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CSS width and height define its displayed box.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Confusing the two sizes produces blurred output, stretched coordinates, or
excessive memory use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="drawing-buffer-and-display-size"&gt;
 Drawing Buffer and Display Size
 &lt;a href="#drawing-buffer-and-display-size" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canvas attributes contain unitless pixel counts:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-html" data-lang="html"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;canvas&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;800&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;400&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;canvas&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The default drawing buffer is 300 by 150 pixels. CSS can display that buffer
at another size:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;css&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-css" data-lang="css"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;canvas&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;inline-size&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;block-size&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;auto&lt;/span&gt;;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;When the CSS box and drawing buffer have different aspect ratios, the browser
stretches the bitmap. Writing &lt;code&gt;width=&amp;quot;800px&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt; is invalid in intent because the
attribute is an integer, not a CSS length.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>JavaScript Script Loading</title><link>https://example.org/javascript-script-loading/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/javascript-script-loading/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The HTML parser, script fetcher, and JavaScript engine can work concurrently,
but execution constraints differ by script type and attributes. Choose a mode
from the dependency graph and readiness contract rather than adding &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; or
&lt;code&gt;defer&lt;/code&gt; only as a performance hint.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>TypeScript Enums and Value Types</title><link>https://example.org/typescript-enums-and-value-types/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/typescript-enums-and-value-types/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A closed set can require a compile-time constraint, a runtime lookup object, a
wire representation, or a domain object with validated behavior. TypeScript
offers different representations because those requirements are not
equivalent.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The npm Ecosystem</title><link>https://example.org/npm-ecosystem/</link><pubDate>Thu, 03 Aug 2023 06:51:10 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/npm-ecosystem/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;npm is the package manager distributed with Node.js. It installs packages, runs project scripts, publishes packages to registries, and records dependency resolutions so a team can reproduce an application build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="package-metadata"&gt;
 Package Metadata
 &lt;a href="#package-metadata" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every npm project is described by &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;. Its most important fields identify the package, define scripts, and declare dependencies:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-json" data-lang="json"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;{
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;example-service&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;private&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;type&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;module&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;scripts&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;test&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;node --test&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;start&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;node src/server.js&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; },
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;dependencies&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;fastify&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;^5.0.0&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; },
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;devDependencies&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;typescript&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;^5.0.0&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; },
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;engines&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;#34;node&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;gt;=20&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;dependencies&lt;/code&gt; are needed in production. &lt;code&gt;devDependencies&lt;/code&gt; support development, testing, or builds. A package marked &lt;code&gt;private: true&lt;/code&gt; cannot accidentally be published.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>